We are in the process of changing the Zelig website to a new zeligproject.org site, coming in mid August. Our apologies that the old site is out of date (it will be removed when the new site is up). As you already found on your own, the latest on Zelig is in Github, which is mostly all new code as part of Zelig 5 (with an entire new architecture):

https://github.com/IQSS/Zelig5

The Dev version is still in alpha, while we are finishing testing and documentation.

